<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edirne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edirne, the ancient Adrianople, is a city in European <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> near the Greek and Bulgarian borders. It served as the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-constantinople">conquest of Constantinople</a> in 1453, and it is home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selimiye-mosque">Selimiye Mosque</a>, regarded as a masterpiece of the architect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mimar-sinan">Mimar Sinan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edirne.jpg" alt="Edirne" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tevfik Teker · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Selimiye_Mosque_and_The_Statue_of_Architect_Sinan_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
